# Tuned tier: the Otter storage, because cache-handler logs that its default
# storage is "not optimized and for development purpose" (Souin storages
# docs), and stale serving for 5 minutes ("stale" in the Souin Caddy docs).
# Otter's size is raised from its default of 10000 (README,
# "otter.configuration.size"): with the default, 5000 stored URLs were already
# being evicted, and sync-expiry counted the evictions as origin calls. Room
# to store the test's keys is plumbing, as nginx's max_size and Varnish's
# storage size are (docs/11 R1).
# The API block and the admin endpoint are as in the default tier.
{
	auto_https off
	admin :2019
	cache {
		api {
			souin
		}
		otter {
			configuration {
				size 1000000
			}
		}
		stale 5m
	}
}
:8080 {
	cache
	reverse_proxy origin:9000
}
